      "name": "Prima Variante",
      "story": "The first chicane, built in 1972 to slow cars before the Curva Grande, rebuilt as a double chicane in 1976 and in 2000 as today’s right-left. Prima variante means first chicane; rettifilo, as in its older name Variante del Rettifilo, means straight.",
