      "name": "Seconda Curva di Lesmo",
      "subtitle": "Lesmo 2",
      "story": "Known as the Curva dei 100 Metri in 1922, and in 1927 as the Curva del Bosco dei Cervi, after the park’s deer. It was tightened in 1994–95. The very slight left that follows, the Curva del Serraglio, is not counted as a corner; it is named after a royal hunting lodge in the park.",
